    "result_text": "The full suite is green (this project's Surefire runs the `AcceptanceTest`, the only test present). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, emitted alongside the existing audit line on a successful owner create.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Monotonic sequence counter** \u2014 a process-wide `AtomicLong AUDIT_SEQ` so `seq` increases monotonically across all creates.\n\n2. **Immutable event record** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent(seq, ownerId, identifier, membershipLevel)`, a private record with a `toJson()` that produces the exact shape `{\"seq\":\u2026,\"ownerId\":\u2026,\"customerCode\":\u2026,\"membershipLevel\":\u2026,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` (with proper JSON string escaping).\n\n3. **Primary-identifier indirection** \u2014 a `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that today returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`. The record populates the event's `customerCode` field from this accessor, so the design guidance in the spec is honored: when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only `primaryIdentifier` changes and the event automatically carries the memberId instead.\n\n4. **Emission** \u2014 after the existing `AUDIT.info(\"owner created \u2026\")` line, a second `AUDIT.info(...)` emits the JSON via the single-arg overload (no SLF4J placeholder substitution, so the JSON braces are safe).\n\nVerified output:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` assertion (one AUDIT line containing `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode) passes, and the build is green.",
